<p>(1) Assumes the shares of the Company issued to PIE in the Combination were outstanding for all periods presented and assuming the shares of the Company outstanding prior to the Combination were issued as of the closing date of the Combination.</p>
<p>Net sales for the quarter ended June 29, 1997, were $43,958,000, an increase of 33% over pro forma combined net sales of FEI and PEO for the prior year second quarter of $33,058,000.  For the six months ended June 29, 1997, net sales were $76,025,000, an increase of 27% over pro forma combined net sales of $59,887,000 for the same period in 1996. Backlog at August 1, 1997 was $49,750,000 (Guilder exchange rate of 2.068) as compared to $39,350,000 at August 1, 1996 (Guilder exchange rate of 1.653) on a pro forma combined basis.</p>
<p>Net income for the quarter was $2,235,000, with net income per share of $0.13.  For the six months ended June 29, 1997, net loss was $(42,000,000), with net loss per share of $(2.72).</p>
